{
  "id": "inw5e2r",
  "title": "CHAPTER 11 – ENERGY",
  "order": 104,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "xkcw4o2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "INTRODUCTION TO ENERGY"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Energy is defined as the capacity to do work, and its SI unit is the Joule (J).",
        "Mechanical energy is the combined total of Kinetic Energy (KE = 1/2 mv²) and Potential Energy (PE = mgh).",
        "The Law of Conservation of Energy dictates that energy can neither be created nor destroyed, only transformed from one form to another.",
        "The commercial unit of electrical energy is kilowatt-hour (kWh), equivalent to 3.6 × 10⁶ Joules.",
        "Energy sources are classified into inexhaustible Renewable sources (solar, wind) and finite Non-Renewable sources (coal, petroleum)."
      ],
      "id": "by1kjxj"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "SI Unit",
          "value": "Joule (J)",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Commercial Unit",
          "value": "1 kWh = 3.6 × 10⁶ J",
          "icon": "clock"
        },
        {
          "label": "Mechanical Energy",
          "value": "KE + PE",
          "icon": "check"
        },
        {
          "label": "Governing Law",
          "value": "Conservation of Energy",
          "icon": "award"
        }
      ],
      "id": "2vusstx"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i5g7y8f",
      "content": "Energy is defined as the capacity of a body to do work. Without energy, no activity in the universe is possible."
    },
    {
      "id": "h6pe9kd",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "oofg0q6",
      "src": "/books/Guide/GENERAL KNOWLEDGE/images/image_oofg0q6.png"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x6o4l4f",
      "content": "Every action in our daily life requires energy, such as:"
    },
    {
      "id": "fpazbr6",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Walking</li><li>Running</li><li>Cooking food</li><li>Driving vehicles</li><li>Using electrical appliances</li></ul>",
        "Walking",
        "Running",
        "Cooking food",
        "Driving vehicles",
        "Using electrical appliances"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y9yf02x",
      "content": "Energy exists in different forms and can be converted from one form to another."
    },
    {
      "id": "ngxzbon",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "UNIT OF ENERGY"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o10at1p",
      "content": "The SI unit of energy is Joule (J)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "oqapi1g",
      "content": "1 Joule is defined as the amount of energy required to move a body through a distance of 1 metre when a force of 1 Newton is applied."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fibcdzz",
      "content": "Other important units of energy:"
    },
    {
      "id": "9whr7af",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Calorie</li><li>Kilowatt-hour (kWh)</li></ul>",
        "Calorie",
        "Kilowatt-hour (kWh)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g1evw48",
      "content": "Commercial unit of electrical energy = kilowatt-hour (kWh)"
    },
    {
      "id": "q11bsxw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "FORMS OF ENERGY"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dtak1fk",
      "content": "Energy exists in many forms. Some important forms are:"
    },
    {
      "id": "5oddbq2",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Mechanical Energy</li><li>Heat Energy</li><li>Light Energy</li><li>Electrical Energy</li><li>Chemical Energy</li><li>Nuclear Energy</li></ul>",
        "Mechanical Energy",
        "Heat Energy",
        "Light Energy",
        "Electrical Energy",
        "Chemical Energy",
        "Nuclear Energy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mwu79sq",
      "content": "Among these, mechanical energy is the most important in physics."
    },
    {
      "id": "16jcvpj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "MECHANICAL ENERGY"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jqpx4rv",
      "content": "Mechanical energy is the energy possessed by an object due to its motion or position. Mechanical energy is of two types:"
    },
    {
      "id": "gg7uuth",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Kinetic Energy",
        "Potential Energy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "hfc1w8x",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "KINETIC ENERGY"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r3q3lux",
      "content": "Kinetic energy is the energy possessed by a body due to its motion. Formula:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "sza22z7",
      "content": "KE = ½ mv²"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x1tvdy2",
      "content": "Where:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qq16cnq",
      "content": "m = mass of the body"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "05gguci",
      "content": "v = velocity of the body"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lylhv62",
      "content": "Important points:"
    },
    {
      "id": "8el615c",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Greater the mass → greater the kinetic energy",
        "Greater the velocity → greater the kinetic energy",
        "If velocity doubles, kinetic energy becomes four times"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z7zq4t5",
      "content": "Examples:"
    },
    {
      "id": "oibhzyj",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Moving car",
        "Flowing river",
        "Flying bird"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2husljn",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "POTENTIAL ENERGY"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Energy can neither be created nor be destroyed, it can only be transformed from one form to another.",
      "id": "34etkza"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "blp6qyn",
      "content": "Potential energy is the energy possessed by a body due to its position or shape. Formula:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "2nvz85l",
      "content": "PE = mgh"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ll8hoep",
      "content": "Where:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "s6atvup",
      "content": "m = mass"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wh5a48y",
      "content": "g = acceleration due to gravity"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "246gkvn",
      "content": "h = height"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xnx73tl",
      "content": "Examples:"
    },
    {
      "id": "pzrvim9",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Water stored in a dam",
        "Raised hammer QCOMPARE",
        "Stretched spring"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nc7eji4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "RELATION BETWEEN KE AND PE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dhcrb3y",
      "content": "When an object falls from a height:"
    },
    {
      "id": "twach5c",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>At top → Maximum Potential Energy, Zero Kinetic Energy</li><li>During fall → Potential energy converts into kinetic energy</li><li>At ground → Maximum Kinetic Energy, Minimum Potential Energy Total energy remains constant.</li></ul>",
        "At top → Maximum Potential Energy, Zero Kinetic Energy",
        "During fall → Potential energy converts into kinetic energy",
        "At ground → Maximum Kinetic Energy, Minimum Potential Energy Total energy remains constant."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "v6ahcp6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "LAW OF CONSERVATION OF ENERGY"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vhtopm0",
      "content": "According to the law of conservation of energy: "
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e9pm6qt",
      "content": "Energy can neither be created nor destroyed."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jo4l4mm",
      "content": "It can only be transformed from one form to another."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Feature",
        "Renewable Energy Sources",
        "Non-Renewable Energy Sources"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Availability",
          "Inexhaustible; continuously replenished naturally",
          "Exhaustible; limited reserves that deplete with use"
        ],
        [
          "Environmental Impact",
          "Clean energy with minimal carbon footprint",
          "Causes high pollution and greenhouse gas emissions"
        ],
        [
          "Examples",
          "Solar, Wind, Hydroelectric, Geothermal",
          "Coal, Crude Oil, Natural Gas, Nuclear Fuels"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "mdvl5av"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cpxkwxh",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i2ebywc",
      "content": "In an electric bulb:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "krydkbl",
      "content": "Electrical energy → Heat energy + Light energy"
    },
    {
      "id": "p2nl5v7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "COMMERCIAL UNIT OF ENERGY"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g0v02rl",
      "content": "Electrical energy consumed in homes is measured in kilowatt-hour (kWh). 1 unit = 1 kWh"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rymk7vx",
      "content": "1 kWh = 3.6 × 10⁶ Joules"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rzmsdfx",
      "content": "Electricity bill is calculated on the basis of kWh."
    },
    {
      "id": "bps6e9k",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SOURCES OF ENERGY"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4br9dsg",
      "content": "Sources of energy are divided into two types:"
    },
    {
      "id": "mpvxigx",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Renewable Sources of Energy",
        "Non-Renewable Sources of Energy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "rlt3dgb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Renewable Sources"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cvk7ndx",
      "content": "Renewable sources are those which can be used again and again. Examples:"
    },
    {
      "id": "27wpima",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Solar energy</li><li>Wind energy</li><li>Hydroelectric energy</li><li>Biogas</li></ul>",
        "Solar energy",
        "Wind energy",
        "Hydroelectric energy",
        "Biogas"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "igms2wh",
      "content": "Advantages:"
    },
    {
      "id": "52cww26",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Eco-friendly</li><li>Inexhaustible</li><li>Less pollution</li></ul>",
        "Eco-friendly",
        "Inexhaustible",
        "Less pollution"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ax4otzu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Non-Renewable Sources"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bxswaw9",
      "content": "Non-renewable sources are limited in quantity. Examples:"
    },
    {
      "id": "40sm972",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Coal</li><li>Petroleum</li><li>Natural gas</li><li>Nuclear fuel</li></ul>",
        "Coal",
        "Petroleum",
        "Natural gas",
        "Nuclear fuel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ei12wif",
      "content": "Disadvantages:"
    },
    {
      "id": "k5ioi3o",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Limited supply</li><li>Cause pollution</li><li>Lead to global warming</li></ul>",
        "Limited supply",
        "Cause pollution",
        "Lead to global warming"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Numerical Conversion: 1 kWh = 3.6 × 10⁶ J (frequently asked in multiple-choice questions).",
        "Velocity Impact: Doubling the velocity of a moving object increases its Kinetic Energy by 4 times (KE ∝ v²).",
        "Energy Transformation in Free Fall: Potential energy converts entirely into kinetic energy just before striking the ground."
      ],
      "id": "1irsrjh"
    },
    {
      "id": "s0z2a6f",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "CHARACTERISTICS OF A GOOD SOURCE OF ENERGY"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "irh6iw4",
      "content": "A good source of energy should:"
    },
    {
      "id": "11onqm7",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Be easily available</li><li>Be economical</li><li>Have high energy output</li><li>Be easy to store and transport</li><li>Cause minimum pollution</li></ul>",
        "Be easily available",
        "Be economical",
        "Have high energy output",
        "Be easy to store and transport",
        "Cause minimum pollution"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "5sakehe",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "IMPORTANT  EXAM QUESTIONS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "829nply",
      "content": "Q1. SI unit of energy? Ans: Joule"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "prq1erj",
      "content": "Q2. Formula of kinetic energy? Ans: ½ mv²"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c54pxp0",
      "content": "Q3. Commercial unit of electricity? Ans: kWh"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0lsquc2",
      "content": "Q4. Energy stored in dam? Ans: Potential energy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "31wap1o",
      "content": "Q5. Law of conservation of energy states?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1zr9iiy",
      "content": "Ans: Energy can neither be created nor destroyed"
    },
    {
      "id": "j6idgcp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "QUICK REVISION"
    },
    {
